Package: simonnote
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Fast tabbed text editor for GNOME
 Simon-Note is a text editor written in Rust with GTK4 and LibAdwaita, made for
 Ubuntu and GNOME. It has a native GNOME look, opens and edits UTF-8 text files
 and uses windowed loading so that large files stay responsive.
 .
 Features:
 .
  * Tabbed editor: every file opens in its own tab, with a close button and a
   dot marking unsaved changes.
 .
  * Windowed loading: large files are not loaded entirely into memory, but in
   blocks of 20,000 lines that slide as you navigate. A 30 MB file needs about
   14 MB instead of 240 MB.
 .
  * Safe closing: if there are unsaved changes you are asked whether to save
   them; choosing "Save" writes the file and closes the editor.
 .
  * Native GNOME style: header bar, light and dark theme, About window.
 .
  * Asynchronous I/O: reading and writing happen in the background, so the
   interface always stays responsive.
 .
  * Undo and redo (Ctrl+Z / Ctrl+Shift+Z).
 .
  * Keyboard shortcuts for every main operation.
 .
  * Several files from the command line: each one opens in its own tab.
 .
  * Status bar with lines, size, cursor position and current window.
 .
  * Toasts confirming a save or reporting an error.
